# behavior: two modules of one dependency declare a model and a union alias with the same names at the same source positions; imported under aliases, each module's union accepts its own model and the consumer keeps the two apart
# retires: loaves/compiler/incan_emit/src/emit/native_unions.rs::emitted_union_publication_is_scoped_to_module_and_span
# retires: loaves/compiler/incan_emit/src/emit/native_unions.rs::native_union_local_nominals_keep_module_identity_through_forwarding
# expect-stdout:
#   first product 1
#   first number 2
#   second product two
#   second number 3

# ROUTE BUG CANDIDATE: baking the provider stops at an emission invariant ("emitted union ... binds Product to two
# canonical identities"): its `first` and `second` modules declare `Product` and `Answer = Product | int` at the same
# source positions. Found when `emit_dependency_unions_and_surfaces` first ran, where this project was a fixture.
# Lands there again when the provider bakes.

from pub::producer.first import Product as FirstProduct, label as first_label
from pub::producer.second import Product as SecondProduct, label as second_label


def main() -> None:
    println(first_label(FirstProduct(value=1)))
    println(first_label(2))
    println(second_label(SecondProduct(value="two")))
    println(second_label(3))
